# =====================================================================
# Qwen 3.8 27B EXL3 3.5bpw + DFlash2 EXL3 5.0bpw draft, exllamav3
# (MiaAI-Lab fork 1.4.2) @ 131072 ctx/request, batch-1 -- 2026-09-04.
# THIS IS THE PRODUCTION PROFILE. Service: uap-exl3-server.service ->
# /home/cogtek/Qwen3.8-EXL3-kit/start.sh
# Install: this is a REFERENCE copy; the live file is the kit's .env at
#   /home/cogtek/Qwen3.8-EXL3-kit/.env
#
# Supersedes config/llama-profiles/qwen38-27b-dflash2.env (kept as the
# rollback profile). Same base model, same per-request context -- the
# serving engine changes: GGUF/llama.cpp -> EXL3/exllamav3.
#
# MEASURED on the RTX 3090 (sm_86) after cutover 2026-09-04:
#   decode, short ctx, warm:   ~82 tok/s  (vs ~55 llama.cpp baseline,
#                              same 600-word essay probe, 1192 tokens)
#   decode, deep long ctx:     ~41-51 tok/s (KV cache growth falloff)
#   VRAM resident:             20964 MiB / 24576 MiB
#   model load:                < 90 s
#   tool calling:              native OpenAI-style tool_calls, verified
#
# 3090 (sm_86) CAVEATS -- do not copy the 4090 recipe blindly:
#   * CACHE_QUANT=nvfp4 / fp8 need CC >= 8.9 (Ada/Hopper). sm_86 is fixed
#     in hardware; CACHE_QUANT=4 (Hadamard int4) is the same ~4.5
#     bits/elem and is what runs.
#   * nvcc is 12.4 (deb layout at /usr/bin, no /usr/local/cuda), so torch
#     is pinned to cu124 wheels and CUDA_HOME=/usr.
#   * The engine fork needs triton >= 3.3 (ASTSource constexprs kwarg)
#     while torch 2.6 pins triton 3.2 and its inductor breaks on 3.3
#     (AttrsDescriptor removed). Working pair: torch 2.6.0+cu124 +
#     triton 3.3.1 + the torch.compile->identity shim in the kit's
#     tools/serve_openai.py. pip's dependency-conflict warning about
#     this is expected; do not "fix" it by downgrading triton.
#   * start.sh re-runs its bootstrap if its health check fails; the
#     unshimmed import check fails for the reason above, so the kit
#     carries tools/healthcheck.py (shimmed) as the gate. Without it,
#     every start downgraded triton 3.3.1 -> 3.2.0 and broke the engine.
#
# PROXY RAILS (unchanged, still correct): PROXY_CONTEXT_WINDOW=131072
# (--cache_size is per-request here, matching llama.cpp's per-slot 131072
# at --parallel 1) and PROXY_CONCURRENCY_LIMIT=1 (the server is batch-1
# and queues concurrent callers internally). The server accepts ANY
# client-sent model id, so presets (qwen3.8-27b, ...) need no alias
# maintenance -- the llama.cpp std::set alias-ordering trap is gone.
# =====================================================================

# --- engine install ------------------------------------------
TORCH_INDEX_URL=https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cu124

# --- models ---------------------------------------------------
MODEL_DIR=models/Qwen3.8-27B-EXL3-3.5bpw

# --- speculative decoding -------------------------------------
DRAFT=dflash2
DRAFT_DIR=models/Qwen3.8-27B-DFlash2-EXL3-5.0bpw

# --- HTTP ------------------------------------------------------
PORT=8080
HOST=0.0.0.0

# --- cache / context -------------------------------------------
CONTEXT_SIZE=131072
CACHE_QUANT=4
GPU_MEM_GB=22
CPU_CACHE_GB=0

# Box layout: nvcc is /usr/bin/nvcc (deb), no /usr/local/cuda
CUDA_HOME=/usr
CUDA_PATH=/usr
